1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,080
Hello friends in this video I'm going to be following a victorian morning routine written and researched by ruth goodman.
朋友们好，这期视频我会照着一套由 Ruth Goodman 撰写、研究的维多利亚时代晨间流程来做。

2
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:11,590
Who is a victorian expert who wrote the book how to be a victorian.
她是维多利亚时代研究专家，写过《如何成为维多利亚时代的人》这本书。

3
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:19,360
And for a lot of this I'm going to be quoting directly from the book because the way ruth goodman explains everything is so interesting and informative.
很多地方我会直接引用书里的话，因为 Ruth Goodman 的讲解既有趣，又有信息量。

4
00:00:19,360 --> 00:00:25,440
So we begin at 7 30 in the morning and I don't have a maid or a servant so I enlisted my husband.
我们从早上七点半开始。我没有女仆或仆人，所以我请丈夫帮忙。

5
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:28,960
To take on all the morning tasks that they would usually do.
让他接手那些通常由仆人做的晨间任务。

6
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:32,430
This begins with opening the curtains and closing the windows.
首先是拉开窗帘、关上窗户。

7
00:00:32,440 --> 00:00:37,200
Windows were often left open during the night to allow cool air currents to circulate.
窗户夜里经常开着，好让凉爽的气流流通。

8
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:44,600
This was largely the response to the work of a scientist dr arnett who was a respected member of the royal institution.
这主要是受一位科学家 dr arnett 的研究影响，他是皇家研究机构一位受尊敬的成员。

9
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:47,720
And he was a bit paranoid about lack of oxygen in the home.
他有些过分担心家里会缺氧。

10
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:51,830
The idea was that if there was no air current carbonic acid would build up.
当时的想法是，如果没有空气流动，碳酸就会积聚。

11
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:56,360
There would be an experiment they do to check to see how much carbonic acid was present.
他们会做一个实验，检查空气里有多少碳酸。

12
00:00:56,360 --> 00:01:01,640
They'd pour some clear lime water over a shallow dish and leave it exposed to the air.
他们会把清澈的石灰水倒进浅盘，让它暴露在空气中。

13
00:01:01,640 --> 00:01:07,680
For an hour or so and then if they find whitish scum or crust on the surface of the liquid.
放大约一个小时后，如果发现液体表面有发白的浮渣或结壳。

14
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:10,120
It would prove that carbonic acid is in the air.
这就会被视为证明空气里有碳酸。

15
00:01:10,120 --> 00:01:14,400
But sadly this experiment wasn't remotely accurate scientifically speaking.
但遗憾的是，从科学角度说，这个实验完全不准确。

16
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:21,200
It was more likely that the water would evaporate and thus leaving scum of the lime there just from it having evaporated.
更可能的情况是水蒸发了，只因为蒸发就留下了石灰的浮渣。

17
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:27,520
Upon leaving the bed people would usually perch upon whatever the household could conjure up in the way of a rug.
起床后，人们通常会待在家里能找来当作地毯的东西上面。

18
00:01:27,520 --> 00:01:32,750
Most households had wooden floors which would be very cold after having the windows left open all night.
大多数人家的地板是木制的；窗户开了一夜，地板会非常冷。

19
00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:36,600
Especially in the winter I have a carpet in my room but I wanted to go all out.
尤其是在冬天。我房间里有地毯，不过这期我想全力还原。

20
00:01:36,600 --> 00:01:41,670
For this video so here we are with an extra rug for no real reason.
所以这里又铺了一块多余的地毯，其实没什么实际理由。

21
00:01:41,680 --> 00:01:44,120
Once you were up it would be time to wash.
起床后，就该洗漱了。

22
00:01:44,120 --> 00:01:51,840
Ruth goodman says that for most of the victorian period the stand up wash was the standard and main form of personal hygiene.
Ruth Goodman 说，在维多利亚时代的大部分时期，站着擦洗是标准的、最主要的个人清洁方式。

23
00:01:51,840 --> 00:01:56,080
And the start of most people's daily routines whether you were a man or a woman.
也是大多数人一天安排的开头，无论男性还是女性。

24
00:01:56,080 --> 00:02:16,030
And for upper and middle class women it happened as soon as they rose from the bed still clothed in their long nightdresses.
对中上阶层的女性来说，她们一起床就会开始，身上还穿着长睡裙。

25
00:02:16,040 --> 00:02:22,350
A little water was poured into a bowl and a cloth was dropped in and then wrung out and then some soap was applied.
先在碗里倒一点水，把布放进去，再拧干，然后抹些肥皂。

26
00:02:22,360 --> 00:02:27,400
And the scrubbing of the body could begin washing could be done in sections.
之后就可以擦洗身体了。洗的时候可以分部位进行。

27
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:31,720
So one area scrubbed rinsed and dried before moving on to the next.
一个部位先擦洗、冲净、擦干，再开始下一个部位。

28
00:02:31,720 --> 00:02:35,680
And this allowed a person to remain mostly dressed throughout the washing.
这样，人们在整个擦洗过程中基本都能保持穿着衣服。

29
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:39,680
The stand up wash remained one of the most common forms of washing throughout the century.
整个世纪里，站着擦洗一直是最常见的清洗方式之一。

30
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:43,480
Whether with hot or cold water with or without soap.
无论用热水还是冷水，有肥皂还是没有肥皂。

31
00:02:43,480 --> 00:02:48,390
And it provided a fast morning wash that could prepare a person for the day.
这种方式能快速完成晨间清洗，让人准备好开始一天。

32
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:52,120
Funny enough bathtubs did exist but they were not the norm.
有趣的是，浴缸确实存在，但并不普遍。

33
00:02:52,120 --> 00:02:57,680
And really they were just largely used by men and modesty played a huge part in this.
而且主要是男性使用，端庄与避嫌观念在其中起了很大作用。

34
00:02:57,680 --> 00:03:03,080
Men might have felt happy wandering around the corridor of a wealthy house in a bathrobe.
男性可能觉得穿着浴袍在富裕家庭的走廊里走动没什么。

35
00:03:03,080 --> 00:03:09,240
But far fewer women did and if they did they would have felt much too vulnerable and exposed.
但觉得这样没问题的女性少得多；如果这样做，她们会觉得太没有保护、太暴露。

36
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:18,710
So even if women had bathtubs in their homes they didn't really use them they were really only used by men.
所以即使女性家里有浴缸，她们也不怎么用；实际上主要还是男性使用。

37
00:03:18,720 --> 00:03:27,110
Even though daily washing of the body was expected victorians did not usually wash their hair especially more towards the beginning of the victorian period.
虽然人们被期待每天清洗身体，但维多利亚时代的人通常不洗头，尤其是早期。

38
00:03:27,120 --> 00:03:34,560
Starting in around the 1840 s brushing one's hair was no longer considered to be an effective method of cleaning it but it was still thought to be useful.
大约从十九世纪四十年代起，梳头不再被认为是清洁头发的有效方法，但仍被认为有用。
